Rowan was a small, fine-boned man with a blue and green gem set into his throat. He was an enemy of [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]], who killed him, and he came back. What returned wore his shape only at first: it became a mass of mouths, eyes and arms, and it blamed the Weft for his death.

He ran errands for [[People/Althane/The Broker|Tech]], who handed him the artifacts that saw [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] blamed for their theft, and he put them away in a storehouse. When Tech was shot, no one came back for them. Rowan set the gem in his throat and became the thing the Weft met, and he served [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Feep]] in his last fight, shielded by a giant sword that hung in the air. When the Feep died the Weft killed Rowan too; the burst of force that tore the weave where he stood would have consumed him, but a blue portal opened under him first and he was pulled away through it.
